  "body": "`wire-iso.cps` formats coordinates with `fu(v) = trim(toFixed(3))`, so whole values lose the decimal point: `G0 X0 Y0`, `G1 X4.838 Y0`, `U0 V0`.\n\nMany wire controls (Sodick among them, per the Sodick post's own comment and the owner) read a number without a decimal point in the least input unit (0.001 mm). On such a control `X5` moves 5 um, not 5 mm: wrong motion. `wire-iso` is today the only post that writes tapers and skims, so it is the one users are steered to.\n\nEvidence: `out/edm-test-square-3pass-wireiso.nc` lines 10, 14 (`G0 X0 Y0`, `G1 X4.838 Y0`).\n\nDone means: wire-iso writes every coordinate, U/V and angle word with a decimal point (`X0.`, `X5.`), pinned by a golden; or a machine/post option forces it and defaults on, with a test for each setting.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
